Creates a 1200 × 300 blue image.
Adds the title "Top Funding Startups in India".
Adds the subtitle "Interactive Startup Funding Analysis Dashboard".
Saves the file as assets/banner.png.
Can then be displayed in Streamlit using:
st.image("assets/banner.png", use_container_width=True)

A slightly improved version that centers the text and creates the assets folder automatically is:

from PIL import Image, ImageDraw, ImageFont
import os

# Create assets folder
os.makedirs("assets", exist_ok=True)

# Image size
width, height = 1200, 300

# Create image
image = Image.new("RGB", (width, height), (25, 118, 210))
draw = ImageDraw.Draw(image)

title = "Top Funding Startups in India"
subtitle = "Interactive Startup Funding Analysis Dashboard"

try:
    title_font = ImageFont.truetype("arial.ttf", 60)
    subtitle_font = ImageFont.truetype("arial.ttf", 30)
except:
    title_font = ImageFont.load_default()
    subtitle_font = ImageFont.load_default()

# Center title
title_bbox = draw.textbbox((0, 0), title, font=title_font)
title_width = title_bbox[2] - title_bbox[0]

subtitle_bbox = draw.textbbox((0, 0), subtitle, font=subtitle_font)
subtitle_width = subtitle_bbox[2] - subtitle_bbox[0]

draw.text(
    ((width - title_width) // 2, 80),
    title,
    fill="white",
    font=title_font
)

draw.text(
    ((width - subtitle_width) // 2, 170),
    subtitle,
    fill="white",
    font=subtitle_font
)

image.save("assets/banner.png")

print("Banner created successfully!")

Install Pillow:

pip install pillow

Run:

python create_banner.py

Then in Streamlit:

st.image("assets/banner.png", use_container_width=True)
